  reason: "WHY RUST: `gunbc run --arg` is the seed CLI kernel. argv is always text (`CliTextValue`); inhabiting a parameter's resolved type identity is a later, located decision that today lives only in `v1_compiler.cli_run`. Silent String binding was fail-open: `--arg supersedes=2` inhabited Str(\"2\") against an Int parameter. Conversion is authorized from std.coercion type_reference_identity: kernel String/Int/Bool, and the exact std.types NonEmptyStr declaration whose peeled ground is KernelMinted String and whose complete where-population is exactly string_non_empty. A same-spelling user type, a std.types NonEmptyStr whose ground is not kernel String, or any deferred/extra predicate is refused. WHY ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE (gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing): by PURPOSE — silent wrong binding on every `gunbc run` of a v2 entry, including belt_scm_corrective_integrate_cli and fabric/fci1 NonEmptyStr recipes. It adds no language behaviour. The native CLI door (`v2.cli.compile_cli`) has no `run` verb.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete these declarations when a `.dag` driver can receive argv as values AND bind `--arg` text against the entry's resolved type identity — kernel String/Int/Bool and std.types NonEmptyStr whose ground is KernelMinted String and whose predicates are exactly string_non_empty — so the seed binder is not a second authority. That capability is a modeled `gunbc run` on the native CLI. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE IT: a leaf-name table; generic where-peel of any String/Int alias; a spelling match on the peeled ground; skipping deferred predicates; copying the binder into another host file.",
